%n ittallaku kalû marṣāti
#note: Collation of NinNA1 has confirmed Goodnick Westenholz’s alternative suggestion @i{marṣāti} (@bib{RN262@300 ad 2-3}), thus refuting her first choice @i{ana ūmē ṣâti} “for future days”. The rest of the line can now be restored thanks to the school manuscript SipNBSch1.
// cf. L I.4 SB "I" 28

%n [... ūm]ī? ina nasāhi
#note: The restoration of ll. 7f. follows @bib{RN262@302}, only interchanging @i{ūmī} and @i{šanāti}. It is based on the assumtion that the passage is paralleled in the Hittite version, as @bib{RN2365@163 ad ll. 6-7} had already suggested. For @i{ūmī ina nasāḫi} see also @i{Weidner Chronicle} 41 (@bib{RN258@148}, @bib{RN100@5}, @bib{schaudig_explaining_2019@348 l. 51}).
// cf. (Hittite Cuthaean Legend C o i 3')

